  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "USGS CMG G-1-97-BS - Alaskan Biologic Habitats",
  "description": "Sidescan-sonar data collected in 3 areas (EXP1, BB, and COD), and video collected in 2 areas (EXP1 and BB). Robert McConnaughey directed the collection of numerous sediment samples for examination by National Marine Fisheries Service biologists. Notes G197BS This was a cooperative cruise with NMFS. The USGS has the sidescan data and video, NMFS has the sediment samples. Maps of surface morphology derived from sidescan mosaics. Area of Operation : Bristol Bay, Bering Sea, Alaska\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Identify and document seafloor disruption due to trawling for fish.",
